  "implementation_note": "We expose the autoencoder's decoded-pixel tensor 'StatefulPartitionedCall/composed_with_sum/pixels/BiasAdd:0' as an extra Marabou output by passing outputNames=['combined_out', 'StatefulPartitionedCall/composed_with_sum/pixels/BiasAdd:0'] to Marabou.read_onnx. This gives 128 Marabou variables (one per decoded pixel) on which TV and photometric constraints are imposed exactly as in the pixel-space scripts (verify_p1_p4_p5_with_tv_bound.py and verify_p1_p4_p5_with_photometric_basis.py). The TV encoding adds one slack variable per neighbour pair (232 aux vars + 465 linear inequalities) and the photometric encoding adds alpha, beta and 128 residual variables with 128 linear equalities and 256 box bounds. mean(x)=0.5 is enforced via the existing pixel_sum auxiliary output (sum = 64). No script regeneration of the ONNX files was required.",
